---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";

/**
 * This page describes THIS WEBSITE only, and every statement in it is checkable
 * against this repository. The app has its own separate notice; do not describe
 * app behaviour here.
 */
const UPDATED = "30 July 2026";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What this website collects, which is almost nothing.">
  <Prose
    title="Privacy"
    updated={`Last updated ${UPDATED}`}
    intro="This page is about this website. The app will have its own notice, published before it opens."
  >
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics and embeds no trackers. If you
      join the waitlist we store your email address, and nothing else. If you use
      the contact form we receive what you type into it.
    </p>

    <h2>The waitlist</h2>
    <p>
      Joining the waitlist sends your email address to <strong>Buttondown</strong>,
      the service that stores the list and sends the messages. We ask for nothing
      but the address, and we record which language version of the page you signed
      up from so we can write to you in the right one.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is double opt-in: you will get a confirmation link, and you are only on
      the list once you open it. Every email has an unsubscribe link, and using it
      removes you from the list entirely. You can also write to us and ask.
    </p>
    <p>
      We will use the list to tell you when the app opens. We will not sell it,
      rent it, or hand it to anyone else for their own use.
    </p>

    <h2>The demo on the front page</h2>
    <p>
      The four-question demo runs entirely inside your browser. Your answers are
      never sent anywhere, are not stored, and are gone when you close the tab.
      There is no model and no server call behind it: it is a hand-written list.
    </p>

    <h2>The contact form</h2>
    <p>
      If the contact form is connected, submissions go through <strong>Formspree</strong>,
      which forwards them to us by email. If it is not connected, the page shows
      an address instead and nothing passes through a third party at all. Either
      way we keep what you send us for as long as it takes to deal with it.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
    <p>
      The site is static and hosted on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>. GitHub
      processes requests to serve the pages and may log technical information such
      as IP addresses as part of running the service. We do not have access to
      those logs and cannot use them to identify you.
    </p>

    <h2>Age</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not aimed at children under 13, and the app it advertises is
      rated 13 and over. Please do not join the waitlist if you are under 13. If
      you believe a child has given us an address, write to us and we will remove
      it.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask what we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected, or ask for
      it to be deleted. For the waitlist that is one address, and we
      delete it and it is gone from the list. Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this changes in a way that matters, the date at the top changes with it,
      and anyone on the waitlist gets told.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
